# Normalize line endings repo-wide: git stores LF; Windows working tree gets CRLF via core.autocrlf.
# Added 2026-07-12 to end perpetual phantom-modified flags from pre-existing CRLF blobs.
* text=auto
tools/hooks/* text eol=lf

# PDFs are binary and must never be line-ending converted. `text=auto` relies on
# git sniffing a NUL byte in the first 8k, which real-world PDFs happen to have
# but reportlab-generated test fixtures (uncompressed, ASCII-only) do not. Both
# QC-scanner no-text-layer fixtures were being smudged on checkout — verified
# 2026-08-17 via `git checkout-index` into a temp tree: 1386 -> 1454 bytes with
# 68 CRs injected, silently corrupting the xref table of a fixture whose whole
# job is to be read by pdftotext. Stored blobs were always correct; only the
# checkout filter was wrong, so no re-normalization is needed.
*.pdf binary

# _archive/ is retired/superseded doctrine: the majority of tracked files (count: git ls-files _archive | wc -l). Marking it
# linguist-generated collapses it in GitHub PR diffs and drops it from GitHub code search
# and language stats, so a search for live doctrine stops returning retired skills.
# Display/search only -- git itself, the tools/ suite (which asserts on _archive/ contents)
# and every local checkout are unaffected.
_archive/** linguist-generated=true
*.sh text eol=lf
